\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Central bank \highlight\uc2  moves to slow rise of South Korea won. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yeom Yoon-jeong \par \uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Aug 1 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday for the fourth consecutive session to halt a rise in the won against the dollar and dealers said they expected more bank buying of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The won, which ended on Tuesday at 757.50 to the dollar, has risen 4.12 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the end of last year. The dollar had been hovering in a 756-757 range in the past week, a three-and-half-year low against the won. \par \par \uc2  "It is the first time for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for four days in a row," said a local bank dealer. "Its dollar support is expected to continue." \par \par \uc2  Many dealers had forcast a year-end dollar/won rate at 730-740 but a growing number of them now put it at around 750. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of Korea (BOK), stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market twice on Monday and twice on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "It is really rare. We are really surprised," said another domestic bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "We have no comment on the market talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But it is our principle to let the won/dollar move according to the market situation," said Kim Sung-min of BOK's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  division. \par \par \uc2  BOK officials normally deny \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But Kim Joon-il, of state think-tank Korea Development Institute (KDI), said: "I believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not stand idly by when the won rises sharply, considering price competitiveness of our export products." \par \par \uc2  Kim said he believed 760 was a proper won/dollar level for exporters to maintain their profits in overseas markets. \par \par \uc2  The won/dollar rate is allowed to move one percent away from the mid-rate calculated daily based on the weighted average of the previous day's interbank spot trade. \par \par \uc2  The won has risen despite a growing trade deficit because of overseas dollar borrowings to finance corporate investment and official infrastructure projects. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's customs-cleared trade deficit was $7.68 billion in the first seven months of this year, up from $4.38 billion in the same 1994 period. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr81059xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
