\par\par \b \uc2  S.Korea  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  moves to check won's rise. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yeom Yoon-jeong \par \uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Aug 1 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fourth consecutive session to halt a rise in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar and dealers said they expected the bank to continue buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The won, which has hovered in a 756-757 range in the past week, ended Tuesday at 757.50 to the dollar. The won has risen 4.12 percent against the dollar since the end of last year. "It is the first time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for four days in a row," said a local bank dealer, who asked not to be identified. "Its dollar support is expected to continue." \par \par \uc2  Many dealers had initially forecast the year-end dollar/won rate at 730-740, but a growing number of dealers now expect around 750. \par \par \uc2  "We have no comment on the market talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But it is our principle to let the won/dollar movement according to the market situation," said Kim Sung-min, of BOK's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  division. \par \par \uc2  BOK officials normally deny \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  But Kim Joon-il, a fellow of state think-tank Korea Development Institute (KDI), said: "I believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not stand idly by when the won rises sharply, considering price competitiveness of our export products." \par \par \uc2  Kim said he believed 760 was a proper won/dollar level for exporters to maintain their profits in overseas markets. \par \par \uc2  The won/dollar rate is allowed to move one percent away from the mid-rate calculated daily based on the weighted average of the previous day's interbank spot trade. \par \par \uc2  The won has risen despite a growing trade deficit because of overseas dollar borrowings to finance corporate investment and official infrastructural projects. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's customs-cleared trade deficit totalled $7.68 billion in the first seven months of this year, up from $4.38 billion in the same period last year. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's weakness on the international market also helped to push up the won but an "influx of foreign funds heading for the Seoul bourse caused a steep rise of won, especially in June and July," said Kim Jun-kyu, a Citibank dealer. \par \par \uc2  A BOK official said about $1.46 billion has been injected into the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since July 1 when the government raised the ceiling for foreign ownership of local stocks to 15 percent from 12 percent. \par \par \uc2  "This prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soak up abundant dollars in the market. But the greenback is still long," said a foreign bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is likely to breach the 700 won level next year and then rebound slightly," said Kim Joo-beom, dealer of the Commercial Bank of Korea. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr81059w9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
