\par\par \b \uc2  S.Korea  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to boost dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 145 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, July 28 (Reuter) - The Bank of Korea (BoK), \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Seoul \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the the dollar against the won, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the won touched 756.50 to the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The BoK \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market when the dollar touched 756.50 won as the U.S. unit was likely to fall further (against the won) due to end-month export negotiations," a foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials declined comment. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened 756.20 and closed the morning session at 756.70 after touching a high of 756.90 on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely in the afternoon if the dollar falls below the 756.50 level. \par \par \uc2  -- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5649 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr7s05f0x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
