\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Korea Buys Dollars, Causing Dollar Rebound Vs. Won \b0\par\par\uc2 117 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1995\par 04:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SEOUL (AP-DJ)--\b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday buying dollars at 760.70 won at about 0100 GMT, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars massively,' said a trader at a local bank. 'As a result, the dollar is quoted at 764.00 won at 0220 GMT.' \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened 760.80 won and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it dropped to 760.70 won, they said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to slow the weakening of the dollar against the Korean won, they said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-06-95 \par \par \uc2  0233GMT \par \par \uc2  1063 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr6904b05\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (South Korea near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\wi